rmation about the rabbit seeing the lion.\n\n8.**Rabbit likes the squirrel.**.\n   - No direct information about the rabbit seeing the lion.\n\n9.**Rabbit sees the bear.**.\n   - No direct information about the rabbit seeing the lion.\n\n10.**Rabbit does not visit the bear.**.\n    - No direct information about the rabbit seeing the lion.\n\n11.**Rabbit visits the lion.**.\n    - No direct information about the rabbit seeing the lion.\n\n12.**Squirrel visits the lion.**.\n    - No direct information about the rabbit seeing the lion.\n\n13.**If something is big and it visits the lion then the lion visits the rabbit.**.\n    - No direct information about the rabbit seeing the lion.\n\n14.**If something sees the lion then it does not like the lion.**.\nFrom the given context, there is direct information about the rabbit seeing the lion. The statements provided clearly indicate that the rabbit sees the lion.\n\nTherefore, based on the information provided, the statement "The rabbit sees the lion" is **true**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
