t":**.\n   - To determine if Bob is not smart, we need to check if there is any information that directly or indirectly confirms Bob is not smart.\n   - From the context, we know that if something is not rough or not kind, then it is not smart.However, we do have information that confirms Bob is kind.\n   - We also know that if Bob is not white, then he is not rough and not kind, which would make him not smart.But we do know Bob is white.\n   - We do have information that directly states Bob is not smart or smart.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - Since we have direct and indirect information that confirms Bob is smart, the statement "Bob is not smart" is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
