ormation to determine if Dave is small.\n\n- **Dave is blue.**\n- **Dave is not cold.**\n- **Blue, red things are not round.**\n  - Since Dave is blue and not cold, and blue, red things are not round, Dave must not be round.\n- **All round things are not green.**\n  - Since Dave is not round, Dave must not be green.\n- **If something is not green then it is not blue.**\n  - Since Dave is not green, Dave must not be blue.\n- **Dave is not blue.**\n  - This contradicts the previous statements.\n- **All round things are not green.**\n  - Since Dave is not round, Dave must not be green.\n- **Round, cold things are not big.**\n  - Since Dave is not round and not cold, Dave must not be big.\n\nTherefore, based on the given context, Dave is small.\n\nThe correct answer is: B. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
