   - The context mentions: "If someone chases the rabbit then the squirrel eats the rabbit.".\n   - This implies that if the rabbit chases someone, the rabbit will eat the squirrel.\n\n6.**Rabbit Chases the Cow:**.\n   - The context states: "If the squirrel chases the cow and the cow is round then the cow is young.".\n   - This implies that if the squirrel chases the cow and the cow is round, the cow must be young.\n\nThe rabbit is not round and red because it doesn\'t chase the cow, and not all red people are big, which contradicts the rabbit being round and chasing the cow.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
