 is red.\n\n10.**Gary is red and nice.**.\n    - Since Gary is red and nice, Gary must be cold (from the given statement).\n\n11.**Gary is not cold.**.\n    - This creates a contradiction because Gary is both red and nice, which should make him cold, but we are told Gary is not cold.\n\nGiven the contradiction, let's re-evaluate the information:.\n\n- Gary is not cold, but he is red and nice, which should make him cold.This contradiction suggests that Gary might not be the only red and nice thing.\n\n12.**Erin is red and nice.Erin is not green.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
