messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is smart. Charlie is big. Charlie is nice. Gary is green. Harry is furry. Harry is nice. Harry is red. All furry people are kind. If Charlie is big then Charlie is green. If someone is kind then they are big. Kind, green people are big. Smart people are furry. If someone is green then they are kind. All big, nice people are kind. All smart, nice people are red. Big, kind people are nice.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is nice.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', 'To determine whether the statement "Anne is nice" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, let\'s analyze the information step by step:.\n\n1.**Anne is smart.**.\n   - This gives us a starting point, but it doesn\'t directly tell us anything about Anne\'s niceness.\n\n2.**Charlie is big.**.\n   - From the context, if Charlie is big, then Charlie is green.Since we don\'t know if Charlie is big, we cannot conclude that Charlie is green.\n\n3.**Charlie is nice.**.\n   - This is given directly.\n\n4.**Gary is green.**.\n   - This is given directly.\n\n5.**Harry is furry.**.\n   - This is given directly.\n\n6.**Harry is nice.**.\n   - This is given directly.\n\n7.**Harry is red.**.\n   - This is given directly.\n\n8.**All furry people are kind.**.\n   - This means if someone is furry, they are kind.\n\n9.**If Charlie is big then Charlie is green.**.\n   - This is given directly.\n\n10.**If someone is kind then they are big.**.\n    - This is given directly.\n\n11.**Kind, green people are big.**.\n    - This is given directly.\n\n12.**Smart people are furry.**.\n    - This is given directly.\nAnne is not nice.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
