ough.**.\n2.**Charlie is not white.**.\n3.**Smooth, black things are loud.** (Since Charlie is neither smooth nor black, this statement is false.).\n4.**If Charlie is square and Charlie is loud then Charlie is smooth.** (This statement is false, and it doesn\'t directly help us determine if Charlie is loud.).\n5.**No old things are square.** (This tells us that if something is old, it must not be square.).\n6.**Harsh things are black.** (This tells us that if something is harsh, it must be black.).\n7.**Smooth, harsh things are hot.** (This tells us that if something is smooth and harsh, it must be hot.).\n8.**If something is square and smooth then it is harsh.** (This tells us that if something is square and smooth, it must be harsh.).\n9.**If something is smooth then it is old.** (This tells us that if something is smooth, it must be old.).\n\n### Conclusion:.\n- Since Charlie is not smooth, and smooth things are not old (from point 19), Charlie must not be old.\n- Since Charlie is not white, and harsh things are black (from point 16), Charlie must be harsh.\n- Since Charlie is not smooth and harsh, and smooth, harsh things are hot (from point 17), Charlie must not be hot.\n- Since Charlie is not smooth, and smooth things are not old (from point 19), Charlie must not be old.\n- Since Charlie is not square (from point 18), and smooth, harsh things are hot (from point 17), Charlie must not be hot\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
